Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.20,0:00:02.50,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the mid-ocean ridge.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.80,0:00:04.90,Default,,0,0,0,,The two paper strips are the seafloor on either side of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.10,0:00:08.10,Default,,0,0,0,,When I pull the strips outward, new paper comes out from here,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.30,0:00:10.90,Default,,0,0,0,,just like new oceanic crust forming at the ridge.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.30,0:00:16.70,Default,,0,0,0,,As the rock cools, it records the direction of Earth's magnetic field at that time.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.40,0:00:18.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.35,0:00:22.50,Default,,0,0,0,,The magnetic patterns on the two strips are perfectly symmetric.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.25,0:00:28.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Now suppose this stripe is 100 km from the ridge and 5 million years old.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.05,0:00:31.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Then the half-spreading rate is 100 km ÷ 5 million years,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.90,0:00:33.70,Default,,0,0,0,,which is 2 cm per year.
